     {
      "id": "6ad86a9cacdd13dd168476f3",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Audition Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an audition form?\", \"a\": \"An audition form is what a performer fills in before trying out for a part. Merriam-Webster defines an audition as a trial performance to appraise an entertainer's merits. The form tells the panel who is performing, which roles they want, and which rehearsal dates they cannot make.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to make an audition form?\", \"a\": \"Write down the parts you are filling and every rehearsal date, then describe them in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form with its time slots, plus a database of every sign-up. Send the link to two past performers as a test before you post the casting notice.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an audition form template include?\", \"a\": \"Start with contact details, the roles a performer wants, past experience, and every rehearsal date they cannot make. Add a headshot and resume upload for acting roles and a vocal range question for singers. If you begin from an audition form pdf, carry its questions into your prompt and leave its layout behind.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an audition form close automatically at the deadline?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if you build it that way. Tell Emergent the closing date and time, and the form stops taking sign-ups at that moment and shows a closed message instead. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/giveaway'>giveaway landing page</a> uses the same kind of cutoff, where entries stop at a set time.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I let performers book time slots on an audition form?\", \"a\": \"Enter when the first slot starts and how long each one runs, and the form offers each performer only the times still open. Add a waitlist as well. Once the last slot goes, later sign-ups join the waitlist and get an email when a time frees up.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I collect self-tapes with an audition form?\", \"a\": \"Ask for a link to the self-tape and the role it is for, and have the field accept only a web address. A link keeps the form quick to fill in on a phone, and the video stays wherever the actor posted it. The panel opens each tape from the sign-up list.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an audition form ask for a headshot and resume?\", \"a\": \"For acting roles, yes. Ask for both as uploads and store them on the performer's record, the way a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/rental-application'>rental application form</a> keeps pay stubs with each application. For an orchestra or choir, ask for a recording link instead, since the panel judges the sound.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I send callbacks from audition form responses?\", \"a\": \"Mark each performer as a callback on the response list, and the app emails every callback the time and the scene to prepare. Performers who are not called back can get a separate, kinder note the same day. Emergent builds both emails from your prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"How long should audition forms be?\", \"a\": \"Short enough to finish on a phone in about 5 minutes. Put each topic on its own screen, and show the singing and dance questions only to people who pick those roles. Forms Emergent builds have no response caps, even for a large open call.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do judges score auditions from the form?\", \"a\": \"Give every judge the same criteria, such as tone and timing, each scored from 1 to 10 on their own screen. Ask for a one-line note with each score, which helps when two performers tie. The panel's sheet is an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/assessment'>assessment form</a> with a fixed rubric, tied to each sign-up.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6adb1e03ceaf35eff3daded6",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Conditional Logic Form FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a conditional logic form?\", \"a\": \"A conditional logic form changes as someone fills it in. An answer can show a follow-up question, skip a page, decide who receives the response, or pick the final page. Each rule pairs a trigger with an action, such as asking for a company name only when someone says they are buying for work.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a conditional logic form?\", \"a\": \"Write down the questions, then each rule as a plain sentence, and describe both to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. Emergent builds the form from that prompt, with its logic and a database for the responses. When you find a rule you missed, add it with another prompt and the form changes to match.\"}, {\"q\": \"Which free form builder has the best conditional logic?\", \"a\": \"No single builder wins for every form: pick the one whose free version handles the rules you need. Tally's help center says conditional logic is available for free to all Tally users. Jotform says conditional logic is available on all Jotform plans, including the free plan.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can I use conditional logic in forms?\", \"a\": \"Use it to show a follow-up only when an answer calls for it, to skip pages that do not apply, and to send each response to the person who handles it. In a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/multi-step'>multi step form</a>, a rule can also move someone past several steps at once. A rule can change the last page too: a large order can end on a different message than a small one.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are good examples of conditional logic forms?\", \"a\": \"Good conditional logic forms let one answer change the rest of the form. A wedding RSVP asks for a meal choice only from guests who are attending. A support form asks for an order number only when the question is about billing. A rental inquiry skips the pet questions when the applicant has no pets.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a conditional logic form check a typed answer instead of a multiple choice one?\", \"a\": \"In some form builders, yes. Tally's help center says you can add conditions on any type of input block. Google's help center says going to a section based on an answer is only available for Multiple choice and Dropdown question types. Before you pick one, list the typed answers your rules depend on, such as a number of guests or a ZIP code.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I put a conditional logic form on a landing page?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent can build the page and the form from one prompt, and a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/video'>video landing page</a> can end with a short form whose next question depends on the first answer. Keep that form to three or four questions, and let the rules hide anything a viewer does not need to answer.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I see which path each person took through a conditional logic form?\", \"a\": \"Look at the answers that trigger your rules. Every response from a form built with Emergent is saved with all its answers in a database you own. Filter by the answer that drives a rule, such as everyone who picked delivery, and you have the list of people who took that path.\"}, {\"q\": \"Why is my conditional logic form not working?\", \"a\": \"Check where each rule sits and which question it points at. Tally's help center lists the most common issues: the logic block is placed on the wrong page, conditions reference the wrong field, or the form hasn't been tested with all answer combinations. After you rename an answer option, check every rule that mentions it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a conditional logic form change its questions based on where someone came from?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the link carries that information. Give each source its own link, such as one ending in ?source=booth for a trade show, and write a rule that reads it. Someone who arrives from a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/qr-code'>qr code landing page</a> can then skip the question about how they heard of you. In Emergent, that rule is one sentence in your prompt.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6acf4f35d1e0031d2648f4ec",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Conference Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a conference registration form?\", \"a\": \"A conference registration form signs someone up for a multi-day program and records what they bought. Beyond contact details, it holds the pass type and the sessions picked, along with the badge name and payment status. Organizers plan rooms and print badges from those answers.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a conference registration form online?\", \"a\": \"Begin with the agenda and the pass prices, then write the questions. Describe both to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> in plain English, including room sizes and any group rate. Emergent builds the form and takes payment through the processor you connect.\"}, {\"q\": \"What do conference registration form templates usually include?\", \"a\": \"Most conference registration form templates cover contact details and a pass type with a payment field. Fewer handle session choices per time slot or proof for a discounted pass. Venue and budget decisions come earlier, on an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/event-planning'>event planning form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I build a free conference registration form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing the form. There is no cap on how many attendees can register. Paid passes go through whichever payment processor you connect.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the limits of a conference registration form template?\", \"a\": \"A Word or PDF conference registration form template collects answers and little else. Each returned file has to be copied into a spreadsheet by hand, and nothing in the document stops two people from picking a session that is already full. An online form records each registration the moment it is submitted.\"}, {\"q\": \"When does a paper conference registration form still make sense?\", \"a\": \"Paper suits walk-in sign-ups at the venue desk and offices that want a signed copy before they pay. A fillable PDF lets people type into its fields in a free reader such as Acrobat Reader. Every return is still a separate file, not a row in one table you can sort by session.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does an international conference registration form add?\", \"a\": \"Mostly a visa section. Conferences often issue a letter of invitation once an attendee has registered and paid, and the attendee includes it in a visa application. In the US, the B-1 visitor visa covers attending a professional or business conference. The form also needs a country field and prices in one stated currency.\"}, {\"q\": \"What to include in a conference registration form?\", \"a\": \"Include the fields someone will act on before the doors open. Badge names go to the printer, and a session choice for each time slot sets the headcount per room. Add a photo consent box if a crew films the talks, plus a required tick on the refund policy. A one-day meetup needs less and can run on a plain <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/registration'>registration form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I move a paper conference registration form online?\", \"a\": \"Yes. List the paper form's fields in your prompt and Emergent rebuilds it as an online form, with each answer saved as a row instead of a scan. Registrations already returned on paper can be read into the same table with AI extraction, and unclear fields go to a person.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a conference registration form template to start from?\", \"a\": \"Each use case on this page works as one. Open the prompt behind a tab and swap in your own agenda and prices. The form usually sits on an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/event'>event landing page</a> that carries the speakers and the schedule.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6adb1c3938ede0a6d1170177",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Contest Entry Form FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a contest entry form?\", \"a\": \"A contest entry form is the form people fill in to enter a contest, giveaway, or sweepstakes. It records who entered, how to reach them, and that they accepted the official rules. For a judged contest, it also carries the entry itself, such as a photo or a short story.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a contest entry form?\", \"a\": \"Write the official rules first, then describe the contest and who can enter in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds the form and the database of entries behind it. Publish the rules at a link of their own and put that link on the form before you share it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What fields should a giveaway entry form include?\", \"a\": \"Keep it short: name, email, a birth date or age confirmation, state or country, and a required checkbox that links to the official rules. Add a phone number only if you plan to call winners. Ask for a shipping address from the winner after the draw, not from every entrant.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I change in a contest entry form template before launch?\", \"a\": \"Change the fields to match your official rules: the minimum age, the states allowed, the entry limit, and the closing time. Then add the rules checkbox and a confirmation message that says when the winner is drawn. Pair the form with a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/giveaway'>giveaway landing page</a> that shows the prize and the deadline next to a link to the rules.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a sweepstakes entry form need different fields than a contest one?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when judges pick the contest winner. If the winner comes from a random draw, the form needs contact and eligibility fields only. If judges pick the winner, add a field for the entry itself and show the judging criteria beside it. Before you add any purchase or payment step, check the rules that apply to your promotion.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I handle duplicate entries on a contest entry form?\", \"a\": \"Have the form compare each new entry's email address with the entries already saved. Keep a repeat as a tagged row instead of removing it, which lets you answer an entrant who asks why only one entry counted. Forms built with Emergent have no response caps. A giveaway that draws thousands of entries keeps every row.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I get feedback from people who filled in my contest entry form?\", \"a\": \"Send a short follow-up form to everyone who entered once the winner is announced. Ask how they heard about the contest, whether the rules were clear, and whether they would enter again, each on a 1 to 5 scale. Keep it as brief as a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/training-feedback'>training feedback form</a>: three or four questions at most.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I pick a random winner from contest entry form responses?\", \"a\": \"Draw only from entries that passed your checks. Pick the alternates in the same draw and in order, and the second name is ready if the winner never replies. Keep the draw record until the prize is delivered, in case an entrant asks how the winner was chosen.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can contest entry forms accept photo and video uploads?\", \"a\": \"They can when you add an upload field. Make it a required field of its own, and accept only the file types your judges can open, such as JPG or MP4. Print the size limit next to the field where entrants see it before they upload. With Emergent, each upload lands in the same database row as the entrant's name and email, and you own that database.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I contact the winner from a contest entry form?\", \"a\": \"Email the winner at the address on their entry, with a deadline to reply and a request to confirm their age and state against the eligibility rules. Once they confirm, collect a shipping address for the prize. If the prize is cash and your finance team pays by check, send it through a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/check-request'>check request form</a> with the winner's details attached.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6acf469800791199561f861d",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Event Planning Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an event planning form?\", \"a\": \"An event planning form collects what a planner needs before booking anything: the date, expected headcount, budget, and venue needs. Organizations use it to approve events, and planners use it as a client intake.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an event planning form?\", \"a\": \"Decide what the answers feed, usually an approval or a quote, then ask only for what that step needs: the date, a headcount, and a budget split into lines. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> makes the form from a plain description, with the approval routing and dated task list behind it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions are on an event planning questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Questions about taste and priorities, once the logistics are known. A planner's event planning questionnaire asks about the occasion and the feel the client wants. Then it asks them to rank food, the venue, music, and decor. That ranking decides where extra money goes and what gets trimmed first.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an event planning survey used for?\", \"a\": \"Two jobs: shaping an event before it happens and judging how it went. Beforehand, an event planning survey asks likely guests which dates and ticket prices work for them. Afterward, a short <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/feedback'>feedback form</a> asks what worked and what to change. Emergent puts no cap on survey responses, however large the guest list.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free event planning form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Template galleries such as Smartsheet offer free event planning templates, and some universities post their own for student groups. An event planning form template suits a one-off event. Emergent is free to start, and a form built there keeps every request as a record you can sort and total.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track approvals on an event planning form?\", \"a\": \"Give every request a status, and record who signed off and when. A status column in a spreadsheet holds up for a handful of events. In an app, each decision is logged against the request, and the organizer can see which sign-off is still pending. The app Emergent builds has no per-approver seats: a facilities manager who signs off twice a year costs nothing extra.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a good deadline for an event planning form?\", \"a\": \"One set by the slowest step, not a round number. Add the longest vendor lead time to the time approvals take. If the venue books 60 days out and sign-offs take 14 days, the form is due 74 days before the event. Guest sign-ups open after approval, through a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/registration'>registration form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should event planning forms be online or on paper?\", \"a\": \"Online, as soon as requests start to repeat. An event planning form PDF prints cleanly for a one-off event, but every answer has to be retyped before anyone can total a budget. Online, each answer is data the form can add up and route the moment it arrives.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between an event planning form and a questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"The form collects facts someone has to act on, like the date and headcount an approver or vendor needs. The questionnaire collects preferences, such as the mood and the must-haves. An organization approving events needs only the form. A planner pricing a client's event can send both, starting with the questionnaire.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should event planning forms include?\", \"a\": \"The date and times, expected headcount, a budget broken into lines and one contact person, plus food and AV needs. Event planning forms for public events add a promotion plan and a link to the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/event'>event landing page</a> guests will see.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6acf53f44d8108b8cce603e4",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Expense Report Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an expense report form?\", \"a\": \"An expense report form is the document an employee fills in to list business costs they paid. Each line gives a date, category, description and amount, backed by a receipt. The finished report goes to a manager for approval, then to finance for repayment and the books.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an expense report form?\", \"a\": \"Write down your spending caps and who approves first. Then describe them in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, which builds the form, a table of every report, and the approval step. Employees then add lines with receipts and submit.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an expense reimbursement form?\", \"a\": \"An expense reimbursement form asks the company to pay an employee back for money spent on its behalf. An expense report can also record company card charges that need no repayment. A travel reimbursement form works the same way for the costs of one business trip. If you repay through payroll, the money goes to the account on the employee's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/direct-deposit'>direct deposit form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a sample expense reimbursement form include?\", \"a\": \"A good sample expense reimbursement form carries the business purpose and one line per expense with its receipt. Add an advance field if you issue cash up front, plus a sign-off from the approver. Purchases that need approval before any money is spent belong on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/requisition'>requisition form</a> instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an employee reimbursement form?\", \"a\": \"An employee reimbursement form covers any out-of-pocket cost a staff member claims back, such as a client lunch or a certification exam. Keep it to an amount and a receipt for each claim. As claims grow, <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/accounts-payable'>accounts payable automation</a> can batch approved claims into the next payment run.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a sample expense reimbursement form?\", \"a\": \"Accounting firms and template sites both publish free samples. The usual layout is a header for the employee over a grid of dated expenses. Compare a couple before you build. The fields they share are the ones an approver expects to find.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free expense reimbursement form template?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Template sites post free ones, and Excel's template gallery includes expense report layouts. An expense report form in Excel is fine for a handful of reports a year. Emergent is free to start, and a form you build there saves each report as a row in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an employee reimbursement form include receipts?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The receipt is how an approver checks the amount and how finance backs up the entry if it is ever questioned. Set one threshold in your policy and require a photo on every line above it. A line missing its receipt goes back to the employee, not on to the approver. Car trips are the exception: a mileage reimbursement form takes a log of miles driven in place of a receipt.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an employee reimbursement form be submitted online?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Staff fill it on a phone the day they spend the money, with a photo of the receipt on each line. Finance gets every claim as a record it can sort by employee or month, instead of a stack of emailed spreadsheets. Emergent puts no cap on how many claims the form takes in.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you automate an expense reimbursement form?\", \"a\": \"Automate the two handoffs that follow submission. The report goes to the employee's manager, who approves it or returns it with a note. Once approved, it posts to your accounting software through that tool's API. Every approver is included in an app built with Emergent, with no per-seat pricing.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6ae99b53c789f9a2869fed98",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"File Upload Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a file upload form?\", \"a\": \"A file upload form is a web form with at least one field that takes a file, such as a photo, a resume, or a signed document, alongside the typed answers. Each file stays tied to the submission it arrived with, and whoever reviews it can see who sent it and why.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a file upload form?\", \"a\": \"Describe it to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> in plain English: each upload field, the types it accepts, and what should happen to the file after submit. It builds the form and the database behind it. The free tier covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a file upload form template include?\", \"a\": \"Start with the sender's name and email, then one upload field per file you need, each with a one-line note on what the file should show. Close with a confirmation screen that lists every file received by name. A file upload form template from a gallery gives you those fields; how files are named and who gets each one are still yours to add.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a free file upload form split uploads across several steps?\", \"a\": \"Yes. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/multi-step'>multi step form</a> can put each group of files on its own screen, such as identity documents on one and room photos on the next. People then see a short list at each step. Emergent is free to start, and that plan covers building and publishing a free file upload form like this one.\"}, {\"q\": \"What file types should a file upload form accept?\", \"a\": \"Accept only the types the person opening the file can use, and set them field by field. A photo field might take JPG and PNG, while a signed agreement takes PDF alone. A field open to every type eventually receives a file nobody on the team can open.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a file upload form work in HTML?\", \"a\": \"It is a form element containing an input with type=file. MDN's guidance is to set the form's encoding to multipart/form-data whenever it contains an input with type=file. Code on your server then has to receive each file, check it, and save it with the rest of the submission.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I put a file upload form on a landing page?\", \"a\": \"Yes. The form can sit in a section of the page or open from a button. For a contest or a casting call, an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/animated'>animated landing page</a> can show last year's winning entries above the upload form. An app built with Emergent keeps every entry that arrives, with no response caps.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a file upload form take files from people who have no account?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the form is built as its own app: it can take files with no sign-in, or ask for one when you need to know exactly who sent each file. Other tools set their own rule. In Google Forms, responders need to sign in to a Google Account to answer a file upload question. Uploaded files are stored in a new folder in the form owner's Google Drive.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I keep files from a file upload form organized?\", \"a\": \"Give each file a name that starts with the submission number, and file it in one folder per client instead of one long list. If you run several file upload forms, add a short code for each form, such as LSE for leases, to the front of every name. An app built with Emergent can also copy each file to any storage tool with an API.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can people upload photos from a phone camera to a file upload form?\", \"a\": \"Yes, when the upload field accepts images. In HTML, the capture attribute specifies which camera to use for capturing an image or video on a phone. To get people to the form from a poster or a counter sign, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/qr-code'>qr code landing page</a> can open it in one scan.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
     {
      "id": "6af427128be8440ad04e1b25",
      "fieldData": {
       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Photo Contest Form FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a photo contest form?\", \"a\": \"A photo contest form is the online form entrants use to submit photos to a contest. It saves each upload as a numbered entry with the entrant's details, and the organizer judges from that one list instead of an inbox of attachments.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a photo contest form?\", \"a\": \"Describe the contest in Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>: the categories, the limit per entrant, and how judges score. For example: \\\"Build a photo contest form for my garden club with 3 categories and 2 photos per category.\\\" Emergent turns that sentence into the form and the table behind it, and the free tier covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many photos should a photo contest form let each entrant submit?\", \"a\": \"Allow 2 or 3 per category for a club contest, then check the total against your judges' time. A club of 60 members entering 2 photos in each of 3 categories can send up to 360 photos. At 30 seconds per photo, that is 3 hours of judging for each judge. Lower the cap if that is too long.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a photo contest form offer more than one category?\", \"a\": \"Yes, once your entrants shoot different subjects. Make the category a required pick from a fixed list. Every photo then lands in exactly one, and judges score one category at a time. For a contest without a photo, such as a recipe or essay contest, a plain <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/contest-entry'>contest entry form</a> is the better fit.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I hide entrant names on a photo contest form from judges?\", \"a\": \"Show judges an entry number in place of the name, then check what else gives the entrant away. A file named after its owner, or a title that mentions them, breaks the blind. Ask for each upload to be saved under its entry number, and keep the title as the only words judges read.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should a photo contest form stop taking entries?\", \"a\": \"Close it at a fixed date and time, and print the time zone next to it, such as 11:59 p.m. Eastern on March 31. Leave at least a week between the close and the results so judges are not rushed. In a form built on Emergent, the app emails your mailing list a reminder 2 days before the close.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a talent search use a photo contest form?\", \"a\": \"No. A talent search judges the person, and a photo contest judges the picture. Use an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/audition'>audition form</a> instead: it records the performer, the role they want, and when they can come in, with headshots attached to the application.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can visitors vote on entries from a photo contest form?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Add a gallery page where each photo shows its entry number and a vote button, and allow one vote per email address for each photo. Keep the public votes and the judges' stars in separate columns to name both a judges' pick and a people's choice. Forms built on Emergent have no response caps, and a vote that spreads past your members keeps counting.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one photo contest form run a new contest every month?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Keep one form and add the contest month to each entry. The limit per category then resets when the month changes. The entries live in a database you own: every member's past months stay in one table, and you can see who entered all season.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where should I post a photo contest form so people enter?\", \"a\": \"Give the contest its own page with the prize, the deadline, and last year's winning photos, and put the form on that page. If the prize is the main draw and the photo is only the way in, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/giveaway'>giveaway landing page</a> fits better.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     },
